@@ -15,3 +15,29 @@ The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Accounts and passkeys
+
+The sign-in and sign-up pages support passwordless registration and authentication
+using SimpleWebAuthn. Signed-in readers can manage their passkeys at
+`/devtools-times/account/settings`. Adding, renaming, or removing a passkey asks
+for passkey or password reauthentication. The server enforces recent verification
+and prevents removing a passwordless account's final passkey.
+
+Account records are stored in `.data/accounts.json`, with salted scrypt password
+hashes and public credential material only. Private passkeys and biometrics stay
+with the authenticator. Astro's filesystem sessions hold account identity and
+short-lived, single-use WebAuthn challenges. Existing password users are verified
+against the original Times login service on their first sign-in before their
+account is added locally. New accounts use the local account service.
+
+Passkeys require HTTPS (or localhost). `AUTH_ORIGIN` can pin the expected public
+origin, without a path; otherwise the request origin is used. `AUTH_DATA_DIR`
+changes the account storage directory. Keep account and session storage on
+persistent volumes. This sample's JSON store supports one application process;
+use a shared transactional database, shared session store, and distributed rate
+limiting before running multiple replicas. Existing remote account creation is
+not synchronized with the local account store.
+
+Build validation: `pnpm run build`. A real authenticator is required to verify
+registration and authentication interactively.
